{#
    Supply-chain security, from Plumb.

    The one question this directory has never been able to answer for itself. extdir
    measures whether an extension works with your Shopware, whether its licence
    permits use and whether anyone still maintains it, and none of those say whether
    its release pipeline can be hijacked.

    Somebody else's findings, and the panel says so in three places: the heading names
    them, every check links to their published guide, and the footer carries the
    attribution their terms require. Displayed, never ranked.

    The checks are listed rather than summarised into the score alone. A number with
    nothing behind it is the black box section 13 says nobody should have to trust,
    and a maintainer reading this page needs the finding, not the grade.
#}
<section class="panel plumb" id="security">
    <h2>Supply-chain security</h2>

    {% if security.state == 'scanned' %}
        <div class="plumb-head">
            {% if security.score is not null %}
                <span class="plumb-score num">{{ security.score|round }}<small>/100</small></span>
            {% endif %}
            <p class="small muted">
                {% if security.actionable %}
                    {{ security.actionable }} of {{ security.checks|length }} checks found something.
                {% elseif security.unassessed %}
                    Nothing to act on, but {{ security.unassessed }} of {{ security.checks|length }} checks could not be run against this repository.
                {% else %}
                    All {{ security.checks|length }} checks passed or did not apply.
                {% endif %}
                Scanned {{ security.scannedAt|date('j M Y') }}{% if security.version %} at {{ security.version }}{% endif %}.
            </p>
        </div>

        <ul class="plumb-checks">
            {% for check in security.checks %}
                <li class="plumb-check">
                    <span class="badge badge--{{ check.status.tone == 'risk' ? 'danger' : (check.status.tone == 'caution' ? 'warn' : (check.status.tone == 'ok' ? 'ok' : 'muted')) }}">{{ check.status.label }}</span>
                    <span class="plumb-check-body">
                        {% if check.guide %}
                            <a href="{{ check.guide }}" rel="nofollow noopener external">{{ check.title }}</a>
                        {% else %}
                            {{ check.title }}
                        {% endif %}
                        {% if check.evidence %}<small class="muted">{{ check.evidence }}</small>{% endif %}
                    </span>
                </li>
            {% endfor %}
        </ul>
    {% elseif security.state == 'unscanned' %}
        <p class="small muted">
            Plumb has not scanned this package yet. That is not a finding about the
            extension: they are still working through Packagist, and about half of
            what this directory lists is still waiting.
        </p>
    {% else %}
        <p class="small muted">
            Plumb reads Packagist, and this extension is published only to its own
            forge, so there is nothing for it to score. Roughly three in ten of this
            catalogue is in the same position.
        </p>
    {% endif %}

    <p class="board-rule">
        <span class="board-rule-label">Source</span>
        Powered by <a href="{{ security.url }}" rel="nofollow noopener external">Plumb</a>,
        which runs these checks and publishes the rule behind every one of them. Shown
        here as reported and never used to rank anything in this directory.
    </p>
</section>
